0a static: rename is registered immediate in the service (no worker round-trip surprises)
1a hero: one primary "Return to Midnight library" on Rooms
1b hero: a "last visited" line from last_entered_at
1c hero: the returning room is NOT the only card (grid below hero)
1d hero click returns exactly once and starts the last room
1e first run: no hero, no "Return to"
1f first run: no primary suggested-action on Rooms
2a chips: exactly All, Yours, Focus, Reading, Late night, Lively, Something new in order
2b choosing every chip sends nothing and has no backend effect
2c All shows every catalogue room
2d Late night keeps late rooms (Night drive, Midnight library, After hours) and drops Northern quiet/Velvet circuit
2e Focus / Reading / Lively are non-empty subsets, each different from All
2f Yours with nothing saved shows no rooms and an explanation
2g Something new includes the authored new room (Finnish discoveries)
2h Surprise me always opens a preview
2i Surprise me within Late night only picks late-night rooms
2j Surprise me never picks a room twice in a row only (varies)
2k Surprise me never starts or changes anything
2l Surprise me avoids the room you are in when others exist
2m Surprise me under an empty Yours opens nothing and starts nothing
2n Something new excludes the room you are in now (history) unless authored new
3a saved room comes first, before every catalogue room
3b saved room carries a Yours tag; catalogue rooms do not
3c a visible "Yours" label exists on the saved card only
3d the active room (Night drive) alone shows a Playing marker
3e four columns at 1200 px
3f cards are 16:9 (1.78 +- 0.12) at 1200 px
3g every catalogue card shows its name and subtitle
3i two or three columns at 800 px
3i2 cards are 16:9 (+- 0.12) at 800 px
4a single click opens a preview page (after the double-click wait)
4b preview shows 'Night drive'
4b preview shows "What you'll hear"
4b preview shows 'Music'
4b preview shows 'Scene'
4b preview shows 'Ambience'
4c preview shows the room subtitle and description
4d Music row for live radio says "programming varies"
4e preview shows the room tags
4f exactly one Scene toggle with an accessible name
4g one primary action: Enter room
4h a note says the current room fades out and other apps keep playing
4i opening a preview is inert
4j preview art area is large (>= 480 px wide at 1200)
4k preview: every icon-only control has an accessible name
4l preview has no internal vocabulary
4m Esc returns to the grid
5a chips, Surprise me, card click, preview controls (scene toggle etc) send nothing
5b card menu offers Rename… and Delete… (and no start action)
5c Rename… opens a dialog
5d Rename cancelled: no command, room unchanged
5e Delete… asks first with a Delete and a Cancel response
5e2 nothing deleted while the dialog is open
5f Delete cancelled: no command, room still saved
5g Delete dismissed with Esc/close: nothing deleted
5h Mix has Save as my room…
5i Save dialog opens from Mix
5j Save dialog cancelled: no command
5k all browse/dialog/menu actions combined send nothing
6a Enter room sends exactly one enter for the previewed room, with_view true by default
6b after Enter room the Rooms preview is gone and the window shows Now
6c returning to Rooms shows the grid, not a stale preview
6d scene toggle off -> enter with with_view false
6e double-click enters exactly once
6f after a double-click no preview is open on Now
6g going back to Rooms after a double-click shows the grid (no pushed preview)
6h double-click with a 200 ms gap still only enters (once, no preview)
6h2 and nothing is pushed later
6i single click previews and does not start
6j Enter on a focused card enters it (explicit), once
6k Space on a focused card previews it and starts nothing
6l focus moves to Enter room on opening a preview (keyboard flow)
7a entering while another room is active offers "Back to Midnight library"
7b the new room is active
7c Back enters the previous room (once)
7d previous saved room named in the toast
7e Back re-enters the saved room via its variant id
7f entering from nothing offers no Back toast
8a main menu has Save as my room…
8b dialog opens with the name prefilled with the room name
8c dialog lists what will be saved: Music and Scene (and Ambience when present) with the room volume
8d dialog has no internal vocabulary
8e dialog name field has an accessible name
8f empty name disables Save
8g Save uses the existing save command with that name and nothing else
8g2 the confirmation toast "Saved Rainy study to Yours" is shown
8g3 Undo on the save toast removes the room just saved
8h the controller now has the saved room
8i the saved room is the first card under Rooms (Yours)
8j the Yours chip shows exactly the saved room
8k saved room preview opens with its name and What you'll hear
8l entering a saved room sends its variant_id only
9a Rename dialog is prefilled with the current name
9b renaming onto an existing saved name is refused in the dialog (button disabled or notice)
9c empty name disables Rename
9d rename sends exactly one rename command for the old id
9e controller has the new name with a re-derived id, and the old one is gone
9f grid shows the new name, not the old
9g renaming the active saved room updates active id and name
9h last_session follows the rename
9i recent history holds no dangling id
9j snapshot (what roomctl/UI read) lists only live ids for saved rooms and active
9k no snapshot field points at a variant id that no longer exists
9l Return hero shows the renamed room
9m Return after a rename still works
9n after a controller restart: variants reloaded under the new ids
9o after a restart: last_session refers to a live room
9p after a restart: recent has no dangling variant ids
9q controller refuses a duplicate name
9r controller refuses a duplicate that only differs in whitespace
9s controller refuses renaming a missing room
9t controller refuses an empty name
9u controller does not rename catalogue rooms
9v renames sent no start command
10a Delete confirmation names the room and says what is removed
10b confirming sends exactly one delete for that id
10c the room is gone from the grid and the controller
10d catalogue rooms are untouched by delete
